+# Wide streaming batches for P1 phasing
+
+This experiment starts from `461aaa0`, the specialized isotropic evaluator path
+recovering 19 of 35 development structures. `wide_fft_batches` is an experimental
+execution option, false by default, requiring `real_fft`. All preceding fast
+controls, including specialized isotropic evaluation, stay enabled in both modes.
+
+## Fresh profile evidence
+
+Three sequential five-second native samples repeat full development solves for
+COD 2243618, 2010647 and 2241159 with the preceding best settings. The first has
+742 collapsed self samples in a native FFT butterfly, 482 in packed-real XY
+packing/dispatch, and 519 in adaptive peak selection. The second has 466 XY
+samples and 640 across its leading FFT butterflies, compared with 580 in peak
+selection. The third has 455 XY samples, 540 in its leading FFT butterfly and
+285 in the FFT radix kernel, compared with 447 in peak selection. Together the
+FFT arithmetic and layout transfers form the largest combined P1 cost in these
+profiles. Their sample fractions are representative, not a full-corpus time
+allocation. Raw stacks, checksums, sampled library UUIDs, exact driver scripts
+and native hashes are recorded in
+`benchmarks/structure-solution-wide-fft-profiles-macos.json` and
+`runs/post-isotropic-phasing-profile/`. No own heavy workloads overlapped sampling.
+
+## Execution and equations
+
+The existing packed-real transform stores the half spectrum in XYZ order with
+last-axis width nz/2+1. Its X/Y operations repeatedly gather eight strided lines,
+call the unchanged RustFFT plan, then scatter them back. The new option stages
+up to 32 lines and streams each packed line contiguously, reducing FFT dispatch
+count and scattered writes inside the packing loop. It allocates a bounded
+32*max(nx,ny) complex staging buffer: at most 65,536 bytes, compared with 16,384
+previously. It adds no full-grid buffer. The half-spectrum workspace still fits
+the existing 18-MiB bound at the maximum supported grid. All grid/input resource
+limits stay fixed.
+
+For line length L, source stride s and batch offset o, the exact permutation is
+
+    packed[lane*L + row] = work[o + row*s + lane].
+
+After the same planned one-dimensional transforms, the inverse permutation
+restores the original XYZ layout. Final partial batches use only the remaining
+lines. These are assignments of unchanged complex f64 values, with no arithmetic
+reduction. Each line uses the same FFT length, direction and plan. The existing
+real packing, twiddles, Hermitian averaging for arbitrary complex input, and
+Nyquist/end-point handling remain unchanged.
+
+The density-to-spectrum convention remains the unnormalized positive DFT,
+
+    F(h) = sum_x rho(x) exp(+2 pi i h.x).
+
+The return operation remains the real part of the unnormalized negative DFT,
+accepting general non-Hermitian complex input. Density-to-spectrum keeps its
+Z/Y/X order; return maps keep X/Y/Z. Normalization is still applied at the
+original caller boundary. Patterson initialization, phase quality scores,
+weak-reflection tests, atomicity masks, omission seeds, peak thresholds, count
+selection, refinements and stopping rules are unchanged. No precision change,
+fast-math, arithmetic reassociation, external FFT dependency or additional
+numerical thread is introduced.
+
+The independent NumPy implementation in
+`python/phasesmith/experimental/solution_fft_reference.py` already expresses
+these equations without native calls; no equation update is needed. Tests cover
+random, constant, impulse and Nyquist maps; both directions; general complex
+return input; tiny/large finite scales; noncubic, non-power-of-two, short/tail
+batches; and all original invalid-input boundaries. Native outputs are compared
+bitwise with eight-line control output and numerically with independent NumPy.
+Complete 80-cycle histories and adaptive/omission decisions are compared bitwise
+for three seeds, random/Patterson starts and omitted/non-omitted masks. Three
+synthetic element-only searches check exact final models, counts and requested
+anisotropic mode. Existing direct density-transfer tests also run the wide
+backend, and the maximum workspace test checks its staging bound.
+
+This changes layout execution of an existing linear Fourier operator, without
+new fit parameters or profile terms. Existing independent physical/refinement
+and analytical-derivative tests remain in the full workspace suite. The pinned
+GSAS-II powder-profile oracle does not cover this single-crystal FFT path.
+
+The diagnostic Rust transform function and private Python FFT/dual-space helpers
+expose the same execution choice. The shared-search audit records the requested
+option and `wide_fft_transforms`, the actual number of packed-real P1 operations
+using the wide backend. Original real-FFT counters are retained independently.
+
+## Validation protocol
+
+The balanced serial runner `benchmarks/solution_wide_fft_interleaved.py` collects
+all 35 development cases under identical settings in both modes, differing only
+in `wide_fft_batches`. Seed zero, four starts, 800 requested cycles, native
+13-second/outer 15-second limits, requested anisotropic final fits and every
+previous fast option remain fixed. Leading mode alternates 18/17 by case. All
+140 predictions precede both reference audit barriers. Seven above-cap
+references remain in every denominator. Adapter-only seal revision 27 inherits
+the unchanged registry and 35/65 split from revision 26 without reopening raw or
+reference data. The 65 holdout outcomes remain unopened. No task-owned builds,
+tests, profiling or kernel benchmarks overlap timed corpus collection.
+
+Criterion `wide_fft_` cases compare the same executable on complete 64-cycle
+32-cubed/64-cubed multi-peak phasing runs and a full eight-atom Fe/C/N/O search
+on 2,108 expanded rows. Actual completed cycles/transforms and full-search work
+are printed in its raw log. Historical Criterion automatic build-to-build deltas
+are not used as paired execution comparisons.
+
+```sh
+cargo bench -p phasesmith-solution --bench solution -- wide_fft_ --sample-size 20 --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 2
+.venv/bin/python benchmarks/solution_wide_fft_interleaved.py --output runs/wide-fft-new --seconds 15
+```
+
+Results are recorded after complete prediction collection, normalized development
+auditing, and explicit comparison with the previous 19-success case set.
